    heiro:2000007 "The NICE manual for technology appraisal and highly specialised technologies (PMG36, 2022, updated March 2026) states that standard parametric and more flexible approaches, such as spline-based and cure models, are available for extrapolating time-to-event data. It asks that the clinical plausibility of each model's underlying hazard function be routinely assessed and that uncertainty in the extrapolated portion of the hazard be explored." ;
    heiro:2000020 "bathtub-hazard" ;
    heiro:2000021 "Concept Architecture" ;
    heiro:2000022 "updated March 2026" ;
    heiro:2000023 "2026-03" ;
    heiro:2000026 "The only PMG36 version of 2026-03, of 2026-03-31, is superseded by the version of 2026-10-13" ;
    heiro:2000036 0 ;
    heiro:2000037 "2026-10-19" ;
    heiro:9000001 hewc:bathtub-hazard .

