heiro:6001652 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "citation of NICE PMG36 in concept critical-appraisal, Concept Architecture, da9f4e"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-wiki.owl> ;
    heiro:1000013 heiro:5000121 ;
    heiro:1000014 heiro:5000145 ;
    heiro:1000025 heiro:4000009 ;
    heiro:2000007 "**4. Interpret the result.** The ratio rises from GBP 15,000 to about GBP 26,667 per QALY. In NICE technology appraisal, under PMG36 as updated in March 2026, an ICER in the range of GBP 25,000 to GBP 35,000 per QALY means a committee must refer explicitly to further factors in judging its acceptability. The claim of clear cost-effectiveness does not survive appraisal, although the corrected result is no rejection either, and the recalculated figure is the one a review should carry forward." ;
    heiro:2000020 "critical-appraisal" ;
    heiro:2000021 "Concept Architecture" ;
    heiro:2000022 "updated in March 2026" ;
    heiro:2000023 "2026-03" ;
    heiro:2000026 "The only PMG36 version of 2026-03, of 2026-03-31, is superseded by the version of 2026-10-13" ;
    heiro:2000036 1 ;
    heiro:2000037 "2026-10-19" ;
    heiro:9000001 hewc:critical-appraisal .

