heiro:6001695 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "citation of NICE PMG36 in concept data-safety-monitoring-board, Concept Architecture, 213960"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-wiki.owl> ;
    heiro:1000013 heiro:5000121 ;
    heiro:1000014 heiro:5000145 ;
    heiro:1000025 heiro:4000009 ;
    heiro:2000007 "**3. Interpretation.** On the truncated estimate the ICER is GBP 20,000 per QALY, below the GBP 25,000 point under which the NICE manual (PMG36, updated 31 March 2026) says recommendations normally rest on the cost-effectiveness estimate. On the completed-trial effect it is about GBP 53,333 per QALY, well above the GBP 25,000 to GBP 35,000 range. The board's stop was justified clinically, but an analyst who takes the interim effect at face value could reach the wrong adoption decision. Shrinking the truncated estimate towards external evidence, or testing the decision against plausible smaller" ;
    heiro:2000020 "data-safety-monitoring-board" ;
    heiro:2000021 "Concept Architecture" ;
    heiro:2000022 "updated 31 March 2026" ;
    heiro:2000023 "2026-03-31" ;
    heiro:2000026 "The version of 2026-03-31 is superseded by the version of 2026-10-13" ;
    heiro:2000036 0 ;
    heiro:2000037 "2026-10-19" ;
    heiro:9000001 hewc:data-safety-monitoring-board .

