    heiro:1000025 heiro:4000009 ;
    heiro:2000007 "In an economic evaluation, the chosen perspective decides which third-party effects are counted, so an effect that is external to one perspective may be internal to another. The reference case in the NICE manual (PMG36, last updated 31 March 2026) counts health effects for patients and, when relevant, other people (mainly carers), while costs are those of the NHS and personal social services. Benefits to other government bodies, such as reduced crime from treatments for drug misuse, are considered only in non-reference-case analyses agreed with the Department of Health and Social Care." ;
    heiro:2000020 "externality" ;
    heiro:2000021 "Concept Architecture" ;
    heiro:2000022 "last updated 31 March 2026" ;
    heiro:2000023 "2026-03-31" ;
    heiro:2000026 "The version of 2026-03-31 is superseded by the version of 2026-10-13" ;
    heiro:2000036 0 ;
    heiro:2000037 "2026-10-19" ;
    heiro:9000001 hewc:externality .

