heiro:6001966 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        heiro:0000017 ;
    rdfs:label "citation of NICE PMG36 in concept incremental-cost-utility-ratio, Concept Architecture, 184116"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-wiki.owl> ;
    heiro:1000013 heiro:5000121 ;
    heiro:1000014 heiro:5000145 ;
    heiro:1000025 heiro:4000011 ;
    heiro:2000007 "Under the NICE manual (PMG36, as updated in 2026), a recommendation below a most plausible ICER of GBP 25,000 per QALY gained is normally based on the cost-effectiveness estimate and the acceptability of the technology as an effective use of NHS resources, and the illustrative GBP 21,000 would fall below GBP 25,000." ;
    heiro:2000020 "incremental-cost-utility-ratio" ;
    heiro:2000021 "Concept Architecture" ;
    heiro:2000022 "updated in 2026" ;
    heiro:2000023 "2026" ;
    heiro:2000026 "PMG36 had 2 versions in 2026 (2026-03-31, 2026-10-13), one of them the current version, so the citation should give the full date. The other dated PMG36 citation in the same record names the version of 2026-03-31" ;
    heiro:2000036 5 ;
    heiro:2000037 "2026-10-19" ;
    heiro:9000001 hewc:incremental-cost-utility-ratio .

