    rdfs:label "citation of NICE PMG36 in concept absolute-shortfall, Concept Architecture, c2192d"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heiro/heiro-wiki.owl> ;
    heiro:1000013 heiro:5000121 ;
    heiro:1000025 heiro:4000012 ;
    heiro:2000007 "Absolute shortfall is one of two measures NICE uses to decide whether a condition is severe enough for the health gains of a new treatment to count for more. The NICE manual (PMG36) sets cut-offs of 1 | In its reference case, NICE treats all QALYs as being of equal weight. Its methods manual (PMG36) allows decision modifiers to be taken into account, either qualitatively through committee discussion  | PMG36 defines absolute QALY shortfall as the total QALYs that people with the condition would be expected to have with current treatment over their remaining lifetime, subtracted from the total QALYs  | The general-population QALYs come from [life expectancy](/concept/life-expectancy) in national life tables combined with population EQ-5D values; the Decision Support Unit guide recommends period life | NICE considers absolute and proportional shortfall together and applies the weight implied by whichever shows the greater severity. If either measure falls exactly on a cut-off, the higher severity le | The Decision Support Unit guide states that the weights are applied to the incremental QALYs of the new technology. PMG36 states that, when decision modifiers are applied, [net health benefit](/concep | The modifier does not apply everywhere. PMG36 states that it is not applied to highly specialised technologies, is not initially applied to technology appraisals of HealthTech, and that a severity wei | A common error is to calculate shortfall without discounting, or with a non-reference-case discount rate, when PMG36 requires the reference-case rate of 3.5 per cent, and the Decision Support Unit gui" ;
    heiro:2000020 "absolute-shortfall" ;
    heiro:2000021 "Concept Architecture" ;
    heiro:2000024 "table 6.1" ;
    heiro:2000026 "Mentions of PMG36 in the text with no version date, and no dated PMG36 citation in the same record" ;
    heiro:2000036 7 ;
    heiro:2000037 "2026-10-19" ;
    heiro:9000001 hewc:absolute-shortfall .

