    heiro:1000013 heiro:5000121 ;
    heiro:1000025 heiro:4000012 ;
    heiro:2000007 "In [health technology assessment](/concept/health-technology-assessment), appraisal is the stage at which a committee or decision body takes the assessed evidence on a medicine, device or test and jud | In the NICE process, an external assessment group critically evaluates the company's evidence submission, PMG36 refers to an assessment phase, and the committee makes recommendations about clinical ef | PMG36 divides the NICE evaluation phase into up to four stages. These are a committee meeting, draft guidance and consultation when needed, a second meeting on the comments when needed, and final draf | PMG36 states that committee decisions are normally based on consensus, and that any vote taken is noted in the minutes. When NICE recommends a treatment in technology appraisal guidance, the regulatio | PMG36 chapter 6 sets out the structured [decision criteria](/concept/decision-criteria) a NICE committee applies. Under the Health and Social Care Act 2012, NICE must have regard to the balance betwee | PMG36 builds this into the decision rule. Other factors weigh more as the ICER nears the top of the range, and decisions must be explained with reference to the evidence, expert contributions and cons | PMG36 table 6.3 lists the recommendations a NICE committee normally makes. Each is matched to how far the evidence supports the case for adoption. | where $NHB$ is incremental net health benefit in QALYs per patient and $\\lambda$ is the value placed on a QALY gain (GBP per QALY). At $\\lambda$ = GBP 35,000 the unweighted figure is 0.60 minus 0.514, | - **Treating the range as a cut-off.** PMG36 says there is no precise maximum acceptable ICER, and an ICER below GBP 25,000 can still be rejected if inputs are implausible or uncertain." ;
    heiro:2000020 "appraisal" ;
    heiro:2000021 "Concept Architecture" ;
    heiro:2000024 "table 6.3" ;
    heiro:2000026 "Mentions of PMG36 in the text with no version date, and the record has more than one dated PMG36 citation, so it cannot be told which they go with" ;
    heiro:2000036 8 ;
    heiro:2000037 "2026-10-19" ;
    heiro:9000001 hewc:appraisal .

