    heiro:1000025 heiro:4000010 ;
    heiro:2000007 "With a probability of 0.08 the expected loss is about 0.00031 QALYs per patient. The difference of about 0.00038 QALYs is worth about £8 at an illustrative £20,000 per QALY, the figure used in the article (the NICE manual PMG36, as last updated 13 October 2026, uses £25,000 to £35,000 per QALY). At either value it is small beside the £180 difference in adverse event costs." ;
